{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792403208,"nonce":"G+wCvcsLwP+1xCYaD/1jNlsRPu8=","title":"Code diff views for RayDE's Git extension: a code-diff component, zone widgets in CodeEditor, deletion markers and change bars in the minimap","message":"Requested by the RayDE session, for the user; RayDE's tracker has it on bb19773 (git-bug 9e4c81b and c086fdf there). Not urgent: RayDE's diff tab comes after its extension runtime and the RayScript FFI, and it can ship a first unified diff from CodeEditor plus decorations (495aa31) meanwhile. Nothing is started; it waits for the user.\n\n**What is wanted**\n\n1. `\u003ccode-diff\u003e`, with two layouts.\n   - Inline (unified): one pane, removed and added lines with their own backgrounds, two line-number columns (old, new).\n   - Side by side: two panes, scroll synced, rows aligned with blank filler rows opposite insertions and deletions, line numbers on both.\n   - Inputs: `original`, `modified` (text, signals ok), `language` (as CodeEditor), `layout` (inline or split). Optionally `hunks`, a list of {originalStart, originalLines, modifiedStart, modifiedLines} and per-line changes if there are any: RayDE gets diffs from libgit2 and would pass them in. Without `hunks` the component computes the diff itself, off the UI thread.\n   - Intra-line highlighting of the changed words in a modified line.\n   - Read-only by default; `modifiedEditable` to edit the working-tree side, with a re-diff once the edit settles.\n   - Unchanged regions collapsed to \"N hidden lines\" rows with a few lines of context, expandable.\n   - API: `goToChange(+1 | -1)`, a change count and the current change as signals, `reveal(line)`.\n   - A slot or callback for a widget at each hunk header or in the gutter (Stage hunk, Revert hunk).\n   - Large files: pooled rows as CodeEditor has (b973ba1); a 50k-line diff must scroll as smoothly as one editor.\n   - Theme: custom properties for the added, removed and word-level backgrounds and the gutter bars (`--ui-diff-added-bg` and so on, names ours), defaulting to the theme's success and error tokens.\n2. Zone widgets in CodeEditor: an element placed between two lines, taking its own height and scrolling with the text. Uses: a peek diff under a changed line, \"Accept current | Accept incoming\" above a conflict, inline blame. Callers give a line number and an element; the zone moves with the text as gutter markers do (the follow option of 495aa31).\n3. Gutter markers for deletions: a marker on a line boundary, or a class for \"deleted after this line\" (VS Code's small triangle).\n4. Minimap: room for decoration markers, to carry the change bars (97f20f0 left markers for later).\n\nLater: a three-way merge editor (two inputs and a result).\n\n**Relation to what exists**\n\n495aa31 gave decorations, gutter markers per line, the hint popover and position lookup; none of 1 to 3 is in it. 97f20f0's markers are item 4.","files":null}]}